s://api.github.com/users/javanna/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-04T07:26:37Z","updated_at":"2023-05-04T07:26:37Z","body":"An alias can be seen as a logical view over an index. The fact that two aliases point to the same index is not necessarily known to users searching against them, and can be seen as an implementation detail. If `alias1` has no filters and has visibility over the whole index, while `alias2` has a filter associated to it that restricts the amount of documents that it exposes, searching both aliases should return all documents that belong to the index and not apply the filter. I understand that this is already case for indices backed aliases, but not for aliases that point to data streams, which I think means this is a bug on how aliases that point to data streams are expanded to their concrete indices and filters.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/1534217216/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"javanna","id":832460,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMjQ2MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/832460?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna","html_url":"https://github.com/javanna","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/javanna/subscripti